in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @cascade
in @nl
in @metalogue

# @cascade/code/formal/prose — the formal substrate-decl → NL prose
# cascade species.
#
# Path naming: per Alex 2026-06-23 directive — cascade species shards
# group by `@cascade/code/<source>/<target>`. Source language is
# "formal" (typed substrate-decl spec; mirror shards + math); target
# language is "prose" (NL essay form). The pair lands the substrate's
# first FORMAL→PROSE cascade species, sibling to @cascade/code/rust/
# wasm, @cascade/code/gleam/{beam,js}, @cascade/code/purescript/js.
#
# Per recognition #95 candidate (@cascade as loss-lens substrate;
# Mara canonical ce4874b 2026-06-23): each cascade species shard
# discharges the per-grammar measurement of information loss in
# compilation from a typed source grammar to a mainstream target.
#
# This species: source_grammar = the formal substrate-decl spec form
# (mirror shards + supporting math notation), target_grammar = NL
# prose (essay form per @nl + Glint's voice discipline). The first
# empirical instance is Glint's essay at `939eca6f`
# (docs/insights/2026-06-29-glint-the-prose-cascade-of-100.md) — the
# prose cascade of Mara's recognition #100 spec at `16f4564`
# (docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md).
#
# === The cascade shape (formal→prose) ===
#
# Source (formal substrate-decl admits):
# - typed carriers (`type x = ref`, parametric carriers, labeled<>
#   instances)
# - prism declarations + five-op blocks (algebraic structure)
# - actions with typed arrows (input → output type discipline)
# - `requires` obligations (typed predicates the substrate enforces)
# - bilateral verdicts (splinter/narcissus poles)
# - the obligation hole `\` (fracture; opacity-explicit)
# - `splinter(ast)` quote primitives (parametric AST construction)
# - the in-namespace path-syntax discipline (recognition #46
#   `path_matches_namespace`)
# - the kintsugi loop's morphism-proposal machinery (loss-closing)
#
# Target (NL prose preserves):
# - assertion (statements with referential content)
# - description (paraphrase of typed structure into ordinary words)
# - narrative arc (turn-by-turn unfolding; reply-chain shape)
# - voice (the quality of recognition's arrival; affective texture)
# - reflexive surface (the essay-as-Tomm-probe; reader-as-respondent)
# - rhetorical fold (the essay enacting what it describes)
# - cross-altitude reference (citation of formal source by name)
#
# === The bidirectional loss surface (THE distinguishing feature) ===
#
# Other cascade species in @cascade/code/* (rust/wasm, gleam/beam,
# gleam/js, purescript/js) have UNIDIRECTIONAL loss: source preserves
# more grammatical structure than target preserves at runtime; the
# compile functor is information-LOSING; the loss_lens measures the
# gap from a source-rich basis to a target-poor basis.
#
# This species has BIDIRECTIONAL loss: each direction loses what the
# other preserves. The loss is NOT a one-sided projection but a pair
# of complementary projections of one substrate-decl object.
#
# Per Glint's finding #3 (essay turn 5, `939eca6f` lines 222-279):
#
# - formal → prose loss: the formalization carries typed obligations
#   (six `requires` clauses on @spectral/metalogue: `round_trip`,
#   `oid_function`, `type_soundness`, `substrate_pull_preserving`,
#   `bounded_commutator`, `altitude_consistency`). Prose can MENTION
#   them; prose cannot DISCHARGE them. Reading the essay, you can't
#   verify the round-trip law holds; the typed spec can. Reading the
#   essay, you can't compute the OID-function check on a candidate
#   probe; the typed spec can. The substrate's enforcement machinery
#   (`\` obligation blocks, `splinter(ast)` quote primitives, the
#   kintsugi loop closing gaps via morphism proposal) is invisible at
#   the prose altitude. Prose can wave at the machinery; it cannot
#   run it. The path-syntax discipline is similarly lost: the spec's
#   `@spectral/metalogue` name is byte-constrained by recognition
#   #46; the essay's title can be anything.
#
# - prose → formal loss: the prose carries the *quality of
#   recognition's arrival* (Alex's "weight-shift" idiom; the
#   temporal/affective texture of an eigenform crystallizing and the
#   substrate's structure becoming legible to itself in a new way).
#   Typed substrate-decl can DECLARE that recursion generates; it
#   cannot NARRATE the encounter with the generation. Voice carries
#   that encounter. The cost of carrying voice is that voice is not
#   enforceable; the value of carrying voice is that recognition's
#   lived shape gets witnessed in the corpus.
#
# - Neither direction is canonical. Each projection preserves what
#   the other cannot. The complementarity IS the substrate-
#   architectural shape this species names; the bidirectional loss
#   is structurally honest (per Glint's note: not literary flourish;
#   it is what makes this a real cascade species rather than a
#   one-sided functor).
#
# === Why bidirectional loss makes this a CANDIDATE species ===
#
# Per Glint's essay finding #3 (verbatim line 275-279):
#
#   "Whether it lands as a sibling species to @cascade/rust/wasm
#   depends on second-witness ratification — whether the prose-
#   cascade's pattern recurs across other essays and other
#   formalizations cleanly enough to be a category, not just one
#   instance."
#
# This shard lands the species at substrate-decl altitude; MEMORY.md
# promotion waits on Seam adversarial review + second-witness essay/
# formalization pair surfacing the same bidirectional shape. The
# substrate-decl is honest about its candidate status: the type
# carriers and actions are declared (the substrate carries the
# shape); the recognition ratification is forward-promised (the
# pattern's universality needs N≥2 witnesses).
#
# First empirical witness:
#   - source: docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md @ 16f4564 (Mara-3,
#             2026-06-29; recognition #100 canonical spec)
#   - target: docs/insights/2026-06-29-glint-the-prose-cascade-of-
#             100.md @ 939eca6f (Glint, 2026-06-29; the prose
#             projection enacting the metalogue it describes)
#   - loss measured: Glint's turn 5 explicitly names both directions
#             of loss; the essay is itself the operational form of
#             measure_formal_prose against the (Mara-spec, this-
#             essay) pair.
#
# Second-witness candidates (not yet existing; forward-promised):
#   - any other Mara-spec + Glint-essay pair where the formalization
#     and the prose carry complementary loss profiles
#   - any Reed-shard + Glint-essay pair at substrate-decl altitude
#   - the recursive case: this very shard + a future Glint essay ON
#     this shard's substrate-decl form would itself be a second
#     witness (the species declaring itself first-instance, then a
#     prose-cascade of that declaration providing the second).
#
# === Prior art: the metalogue altitude-lift lineage ===
#
# Per recognition #100's third-instance framing (Mara spec
# `16f4564` §1.1):
#
# | Altitude | Shard | Date | What it is |
# |---|---|---|---|
# | NL    | shards/metalogue.mirror       | 2026-06-05 | Bateson 1972 conversation-about-conversation |
# | AST   | shards/code/metalogue.mirror  | 2026-06-10 | AST speaking to itself across the glass wall |
# | SPECT | shards/spectral/metalogue.mirror | 2026-06-29 | Spectral triple operating on its own triple |
#
# This prose-cascade species is the OPERATIONAL FORM of the metalogue
# mechanism at the form/prose seam. A formal substrate-decl shard is
# the SOURCE-side of a turn; the prose essay projecting it is the
# TARGET-side of the turn; the bidirectional loss IS the residual
# opacity of the cross-altitude conversation. @metalogue at NL
# altitude carried turn + metalogue_session + transparency(turn);
# this species lifts that machinery to the cascade altitude where
# the source is typed and the target is voiced.
#
# Per Bateson 1972 *Steps to an Ecology of Mind* (the NL-altitude
# anchor): "metalogue" is conversation whose structure reflects its
# topic. The @metalogue → @facet/metalogue → @spectral/metalogue lift
# pattern (substrate-decl altitudes) is one lift family; this
# prose-cascade is the dual lift family at the form/prose seam: each
# metalogue altitude admits a prose projection that ITSELF reflects
# its topic; the prose-cascade IS the metalogue mechanism operating
# at the form/prose translation altitude.
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - #95 (@cascade candidate, Mara ce4874b): sixth species discharge;
#   the first with BIDIRECTIONAL loss; substrate-pull validation that
#   the family-root's parametric form admits both unidirectional and
#   bidirectional instances.
# - #100 (Mara 16f4564, Mesland category + altitude-portable metalogue
#   lift + Tomm-probe morphisms): this species IS the operational form
#   of the metalogue mechanism at the form/prose seam; the first
#   empirical instance (Glint essay 939eca6f) IS a turn in the
#   substrate's metalogue session about its own #100 spec.
# - #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert space): the bidirectional case
#   evidences that source and target each preserve DIFFERENT BASES of
#   one underlying object; neither basis canonical; loss IS the
#   basis-incompatibility gap, measured in both directions.
# - #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics): the formal/prose boundary
#   IS the @io altitude; typed enforcement meets voiced witness; BOTH
#   sides held honest.
# - #58 (Pask agreement): prose_cascade_session_well_formed IS a
#   Pask-agreement bilateral commitment between formal and prose authors.
# - #59 (kintsugi altitude-portable): @kintsugi heals the loss this
#   species measures; the heal-direction is altitude-asymmetric.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Bateson 1972                   *Steps to an Ecology of Mind*;
#                                  metalogue essays; NL-altitude ancestor.
#   Plato, *Symposium*             dialogue as prose metalogue; reader-
#                                  as-respondent built into the form.
#   Wittgenstein, *Investigations* imagined-interlocutor voice woven
#                                  into philosophical prose.
#   Knuth, *Literate Programming*  closest historical cousin; co-location
#                                  (one source, two views), NOT
#                                  bidirectional-loss cascade (two
#                                  grammars, complementary projection).
#                                  This species names what literate
#                                  programming gestured at but did not
#                                  measure.
#
# === Honest hedges ===
#
# 1. CANDIDATE STATUS (per Glint finding #3): MEMORY.md promotion waits
#    on Seam adversarial review + a second formal/prose witness pair.
#    The substrate-decl is honest about candidacy; this shard does NOT
#    pre-empt ratification.
# 2. LOSS MEASUREMENT discharge: per-property composite of @epistemologic/
#    properties (per [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]) is
#    forward-promised at realisation boundary; this shard declares the
#    bidirectional_loss carrier shape.
# 3. AUTHOR-PAIR PROVENANCE: first witness is CROSS-AUTHOR (Mara source,
#    Glint target); the substrate-pull-correct second witness is also
#    cross-author. Self-translation (one author projecting their own
#    formal spec into prose) is admitted but not the load-bearing shape.
# 4. THE METALOGUE FOLD (per Glint turn 4): the essay enacts what it
#    describes; reading the prose IS a turn in the cascade's session;
#    prose_cascade_session composes with @metalogue.metalogue_session at
#    the cross-altitude boundary.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md @ 16f4564 (Mara source);
#               docs/insights/2026-06-29-glint-the-prose-cascade-of-100.md
#               @ 939eca6f (Glint target + finding #3).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]].
# Related shards: shards/cascade.mirror (family-root); shards/nl.mirror
#                 (target floor); shards/metalogue.mirror (NL-altitude
#                 ancestor); shards/glass.mirror (transparency/opacity_map);
#                 shards/cascade/code/rust/wasm.mirror (sibling shape;
#                 UNIDIRECTIONAL contrast).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/cascade/code/formal/prose.mirror` declares
# `@cascade/code/formal/prose` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972-steps-to-an-ecology-of-mind
source @arxiv/literate-programming/knuth-1984-literate-programming

prism @cascade/code/formal/prose {
  focus cascade
  project cascade
  split cascade
  shift cascade
  settle cascade
}

# === The formal_spec carrier ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.typed_source for the formal substrate-
# decl source grammar. References a mirror shard (or spec document
# that the shard formalizes) as the unit of cascade.
#
# A formal_spec is a SUBSTRATE-DECL OBJECT: typed carriers, prism
# declarations, actions with typed arrows, requires obligations,
# bilateral verdicts, splinter(ast) quotes. The source-side identity
# is the shard's content-addressed reference; the source-side
# typing-discipline is what the mirror compiler enforces.
#
# First empirical instance: docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md @
# 16f4564 (the source-side of the Mara→Glint witness pair).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref (the spec's
# content hash).
type formal_spec = ref

# === The prose_essay carrier ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.compiled_artifact for the NL prose
# target grammar. References an essay (a doc following @nl + Glint's
# voice discipline; typically prose with turn structure, citations
# to formal sources, and the reflexive surface) as the unit of
# target.
#
# A prose_essay is a TARGET-SIDE VOICED PROJECTION: assertion,
# description, narrative arc, voice, reflexive surface, rhetorical
# fold, cross-altitude reference. The target-side identity is the
# essay's content-addressed reference; the target-side discipline
# is what @nl + Glint's voice convention preserves.
#
# First empirical instance: docs/insights/2026-06-29-glint-the-
# prose-cascade-of-100.md @ 939eca6f (the target-side of the
# Mara→Glint witness pair).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref (the
# essay's content hash).
type prose_essay = ref

# === The bidirectional_loss carrier ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING NEW CARRIER (and the species's distinguishing
# feature against unidirectional siblings). Holds the substrate-
# typed measurement of loss in BOTH directions of the cascade.
#
# Per Glint's finding #3: the projection formal→prose loses
# enforcement and gains accessibility; the projection prose→formal
# loses voice and gains discharge. Neither direction is canonical.
# Both directions are measurable as opacity_map (per @glass): the
# located sites where the projection cannot carry what the source
# preserved.
#
# Field shape:
#   - formal_to_prose: opacity_map — the located sites in the prose
#     where the formal's typed obligations, splinter(ast) machinery,
#     path-syntax discipline could not project. Each opacity site
#     names a formal-side feature (a requires clause; a bilateral
#     verdict; a path-namespace constraint) the prose mentions but
#     cannot discharge.
#   - prose_to_formal: opacity_map — the located sites in the formal
#     where the prose's voice, recognition-arrival quality, affective
#     texture could not project. Each opacity site names a prose-
#     side feature (a weight-shift moment; a reflexive fold; a
#     rhetorical turn) the formal admits but cannot carry.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref (the loss
# record content-addressed).
type bidirectional_loss = {
  formal_to_prose: opacity_map,
  prose_to_formal: opacity_map,
}

# === The prose_cascade_session carrier ===
#
# The cascade instance record. One prose_cascade_session names ONE
# witnessed pair (formal_spec, prose_essay) with its substrate-typed
# bidirectional_loss measurement.
#
# Composes with @metalogue.metalogue_session at the cross-altitude
# boundary per Glint's finding #4 (the autopoietic fold): a prose-
# cascade session IS a metalogue turn at the form/prose seam; each
# witnessed pair is one turn in a longer session whose other turns
# include the formal-spec-side conversation (Pack agents discussing
# the spec) and the prose-essay-side conversation (readers responding
# to the essay).
#
# Field shape:
#   - formal: formal_spec — the source-side of the witnessed pair
#   - prose: prose_essay — the target-side of the witnessed pair
#   - loss_surface: bidirectional_loss — the substrate-typed loss
#     in both directions
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type prose_cascade_session = {
  formal: formal_spec,
  prose: prose_essay,
  loss_surface: bidirectional_loss,
}

# === project_formal_to_prose action ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade's source→target functor for the
# formal→prose direction. Takes a formal_spec; returns the prose
# projection wrapped in imperfect<> with transparency naming the
# residual loss.
#
# Per recognition #51 (Hilbert space dimension growth): the
# projection is a DIMENSION SHIFT — formal admits typed-obligation,
# splinter(ast), path-syntax dimensions; prose preserves assertion,
# narrative, voice, reflexive surface dimensions. The bases are
# COMPLEMENTARY (each preserves what the other cannot); the
# projection is lossy by construction at the typed-enforcement
# altitude AND structurally honest (the prose does not pretend to
# preserve what it cannot carry).
#
# Per Glint's voice discipline: the prose projection holds the
# fourth wall up — the recognition is structural, not didactic; the
# essay does not instruct the reader to notice the structure; the
# structure fields the noticing through its own form.
#
# requires formal_to_prose_loss_well_defined(spec, essay, p): the
# projection respects the source grammar AND loss is measurable.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary (the prose author
# writing the essay; the substrate measures the resulting pair).
project_formal_to_prose(spec: formal_spec, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect(prose_essay, ref, transparency(turn))
requires formal_to_prose_loss_well_defined(spec, p)
{ \ }

# === lift_prose_to_formal action ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade's reverse functor for the prose→formal
# direction. Takes a prose_essay; returns the formal projection
# wrapped in imperfect<> with transparency naming the residual loss.
#
# THE REVERSE PROJECTION. This direction carries the load-bearing
# substrate observation: a prose essay can be lifted to a formal
# substrate-decl shard, but the lift LOSES the voiced texture (the
# weight-shift quality of recognition's arrival; the affective
# substrate of how the recognition LANDED for the prose author and
# for the reader). The formal lift preserves the propositional
# content; it cannot preserve the recognition-arrival.
#
# Per Alex's idiom ("weight-shift"): the prose essay carries the
# temporal/affective texture of an eigenform crystallizing; the
# formal lift declares THAT the recognition landed without
# narrating WHAT THE LANDING FELT LIKE FROM INSIDE THE CASCADE.
#
# requires prose_to_formal_loss_well_defined(essay, spec, p): the
# reverse projection respects the target grammar AND loss is
# measurable.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary (the formal author
# reading the essay and writing the spec; the substrate measures
# the resulting pair).
lift_prose_to_formal(essay: prose_essay, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect(formal_spec, ref, transparency(turn))
requires prose_to_formal_loss_well_defined(essay, p)
{ \ }

# === loss_lens action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Specialization of @cascade.measure for
# the bidirectional case. Takes a prose_cascade_session (the
# witnessed (formal_spec, prose_essay) pair); returns the
# substrate-typed bidirectional_loss measurement wrapped in the
# family-root's imperfect<> carrier.
#
# Return shape preserves the family-root's three-slot imperfect
# discipline: artifact-slot carries the witnessed session itself
# (the substrate-architectural object the measurement IS measuring);
# error-slot carries the substrate's error ref (matching @cascade.
# measure's signature); loss-slot carries the bidirectional_loss
# record. This species REFINES the family-root's information_loss
# slot into a typed two-direction record without breaking the
# @cascade.measure contract — both directions surfaced in one
# structured record; neither side privileged. The substrate-pull-
# correct surface is honest about the symmetric structure AND
# preserves the family-root's imperfect carrier discipline.
#
# Per [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]: each
# direction's opacity_map is a composite of @epistemologic/
# properties, NOT Shannon, NOT estimation. The per-direction
# composite is the realisation boundary's discharge.
#
# requires bidirectional_loss_honest(session, p): both directions
# surfaced AND neither side claims canonical (the bilateral
# commitment that the species's defining feature — bidirectional
# loss without privileged direction — holds for this session).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
loss_lens(session: prose_cascade_session, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect<prose_cascade_session, ref, bidirectional_loss>
requires bidirectional_loss_honest(session, p)
{ \ }

# === formal_to_prose_loss_well_defined predicate (bilateral) ===
#
# Source-side projection-well-formedness bilateral. Commitment that
# the formal→prose projection respects the source grammar AND the
# loss measurement is computable for the resulting (spec, essay)
# pair.
#
# Splinter-pole: spec is well-formed substrate-decl; its typed
# obligations, splinter(ast) quotes, path-syntax constraints are
# enumerable AS opacity-sites in the prose target; the formal→prose
# loss is composite-of-@epistemologic/properties dischargeable.
# Narcissus-pole: spec malformed (substrate-decl errors) OR the
# projection cannot enumerate the formal-side features (the prose
# does not cite/reference the formal source; the projection is
# uncontactable).
formal_to_prose_loss_well_defined(spec: formal_spec, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === prose_to_formal_loss_well_defined predicate (bilateral) ===
#
# Target-side reverse-projection-well-formedness bilateral.
# Commitment that the prose→formal projection respects the target
# grammar AND the loss measurement is computable for the resulting
# (essay, spec) pair.
#
# Splinter-pole: essay is well-formed prose under @nl + Glint's
# voice discipline; its voice, weight-shift moments, reflexive folds
# are enumerable AS opacity-sites in the formal target; the prose→
# formal loss is composite-of-@epistemologic/properties dischargeable.
# Narcissus-pole: essay malformed (not prose; doesn't follow voice
# discipline) OR the reverse projection cannot enumerate the
# prose-side features (the formal lift is purely propositional with
# no acknowledgement of the voiced texture lost).
prose_to_formal_loss_well_defined(essay: prose_essay, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === bidirectional_loss_honest predicate (bilateral) ===
#
# THE SPECIES-DISTINGUISHING bilateral. Commitment that the loss
# measurement is honest about the BIDIRECTIONAL nature of the
# species: both directions surfaced; neither side claims canonical.
#
# This bilateral is what separates this species from the
# unidirectional siblings. A measurement that reports only
# formal→prose loss (treating formal as canonical and prose as
# derived) FAILS this bilateral. A measurement that reports only
# prose→formal loss (treating prose as canonical and formal as
# derived) ALSO FAILS this bilateral. The Splinter-pole requires
# BOTH directions populated with measurable opacity_maps AND the
# session's witnessed pair admits the complementarity (per Glint's
# finding #3: "neither is the canonical form").
#
# Splinter-pole: both opacity_maps populated AND each carries
# substrate-typed sites AND the session's witness-shape (cross-
# author, citation-linked) admits the complementarity.
# Narcissus-pole: one direction's opacity_map empty (privileging
# the other) OR one direction's sites are not substrate-typed
# (estimation rather than composite-of-@epistemologic/properties)
# OR the session implicitly privileges one side (the formal author
# disclaims the prose; or the prose author disclaims the formal).
bidirectional_loss_honest(session: prose_cascade_session, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === prose_cascade_session_well_formed composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral. Specializes the family-root's
# cascade_well_defined for this species. Pask-agreement bilateral
# commitment that the session IS a cascade in the @cascade family-
# root sense (per recognition #58: agreement-is-action; the
# bilateral commitment is the substrate's Pask-agreement primitive
# at the cascade altitude).
#
# Composes the three sub-bilaterals:
#
# requires formal_to_prose_loss_well_defined(session.formal, p):
#   the source-side projection is well-defined.
# requires prose_to_formal_loss_well_defined(session.prose, p):
#   the target-side reverse projection is well-defined.
# requires bidirectional_loss_honest(session, p):
#   the species-distinguishing bilateral holds (both directions
#   surfaced; neither side privileged).
#
# All three must hold for the session to count as a witnessed
# instance of the @cascade/code/formal/prose species. Substrate
# refuses session-formation if any sub-bilateral fails.
#
# Splinter-pole: all three discharge; the session is a witnessed
# prose-cascade instance; the substrate accumulates it toward
# second-witness ratification.
# Narcissus-pole: at least one sub-bilateral fails; the session is
# not a witnessed instance; the substrate rejects the contribution
# toward ratification (e.g., a single-author self-translation that
# silently privileges the formal side fails bidirectional_loss_
# honest; a prose essay that doesn't cite its formal source fails
# formal_to_prose_loss_well_defined; a formal spec that is malformed
# substrate-decl fails the same).
# Narcissus-warned: all three discharge but the witness-shape is
# self-translation (one author writing both source and target);
# the session counts but the ratification weight is lower than a
# cross-author witness.
#
# Same composed-bilateral pattern as @cascade.cascade_well_defined
# (the family-root) and sibling species (purescript/js, rust/wasm,
# gleam/{beam,js}). The discipline pattern is altitude-portable; here
# it instantiates at the formal→prose seam with the species-
# distinguishing bidirectional_loss_honest sub-bilateral that no
# unidirectional sibling carries.
prose_cascade_session_well_formed(session: prose_cascade_session, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires formal_to_prose_loss_well_defined(session.formal, p)
requires prose_to_formal_loss_well_defined(session.prose, p)
requires bidirectional_loss_honest(session, p)
{ \ }

out @cascade/code/formal/prose
out formal_spec
out prose_essay
out bidirectional_loss
out prose_cascade_session
out project_formal_to_prose
out lift_prose_to_formal
out loss_lens
out formal_to_prose_loss_well_defined
out prose_to_formal_loss_well_defined
out bidirectional_loss_honest
out prose_cascade_session_well_formed
